ble="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="true" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,299][1440,2773]"><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="prayertime.compassdirection.qiblafinder.hijricalender" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[49,299][1391,999]" /><node index="1" text="" resource-id="" class="h4.w" package="prayertime.compassdirection.qiblafinder.hijricalender" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[56,1055][1384,2872]"><node index="0" text='What is Islam&#10;&#10;Islam is a monotheistic religion centered on the belief in one God,&#10;Allah. The word "Islam" means submission or surrender to the will of&#10;Allah. A Muslim is one who submits to Allah, seeking peace through&#10;obedience and faith. Islam teaches that true success and inner peace&#10;come from following the guidance of Allah.&#10;&#10;Core Beliefs of Islam&#10;&#10;The foundation of Islam is built upon key beliefs that guide a Muslim&apos;s&#10;life: * Belief in One God (Tawheed): Allah is the only one worthy&#10;of worship, without partners or equals.&#10;* Belief in Angels: Created by Allah, they carry out His commands&#10;without disobedience.&#10;* Belief in Revealed Books: Including the Qur&apos;an and previous&#10;scriptures in their original forms.&#10;* Belief in Prophets: Messengers sent to guide humanity, ending&#10;with Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him).&#10;* Belief in the Day of Judgment: Every soul will be held&#10;accountable for its deeds.&#10;* Belief in Divine Decree (Qadar): Everything occurs by Allah&apos;s&#10;knowledge and wisdom.&#10;&#10;The Testimony of Faith (Shahada)&#10;&#10;The Shahada is the declaration that defines a Muslim&apos;s belief:&#10;"There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."&#10;This statement affirms the oneness of Allah and the prophethood of&#10;Muhammad (peace be upon him). It is the first and most important pillar&#10;of Islam.&#10;&#10;Principles of Islam&#10;&#10;Islam provides complete guidance for life, encouraging both spiritual&#10;devotion and moral conduct: * Worship Allah with sincerity and&#10;consistency.&#10;* Practice honesty, kindness, and justice in all dealings.&#10;* Support the needy and build strong relationships within the&#10;community.&#10;* Strive for self-discipline and personal growth.&#10;&#10;The Qur&apos;an states:&#10;"Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam." (Qur&apos;an 3:19)&#10;&#10;The Path to Peace&#10;&#10;Islam guides individuals toward peace---within themselves and with&#10;others---through submission to Allah. By following His teachings and&#10;living righteously, Muslims aim to achieve success in this life and the&#10;hereafter.' resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="prayertime.compassdirection.qiblafinder.hijricalender" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[56,1055][1384,2872]" /></node></node><node index="1" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="prayertime.compassdirection.qiblafinder.hijricalender" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,98][1440,299]"><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="prayertime.compassdirection.qiblafinder.hijricalender" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="